    <briefdescription>
<para>A Ginkgo stopping criterion based on the infinite norm of the residual. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The criterion is satisfied when ||r||_inf &lt;= reduction_factor * ||b||_inf, where r is the residual vector provided by the solver at each iteration (for CG/BiCGSTAB this is the residual computed by the recurrence of the method, not an explicitly re-computed b - Ax). Only single right-hand sides are supported.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ExecSpace</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The Kokkos execution space which has access to the Ginkgo executor memory. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
